    "durationMs": 208594,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener API is complete and fully verified. `sh start.sh` applies migrations and serves on 0.0.0.0:8000.\n\n**Implementation** (flat `package main`, ~450 lines):\n- `main.go` — reads `DATABASE_URL` from env, opens pgx via `database/sql`, runs migrations, serves\n- `migrate.go` + `migrations/0001_init.sql` — embedded, idempotent migration runner tracking `schema_migrations`\n- `store.go` — persistence layer: `Insert` (unique-violation → `ErrDuplicateCode`), `Get`, `RegisterClick` (atomic `UPDATE ... clicks + 1 RETURNING url`, so each redirect counts exactly once), `List` ordered by id\n- `handlers.go` — chi v5.2.1 routes with URL/code validation, 8-char random generated codes (retry on collision), proper 201/409/404/422 JSON responses\n\n**Verification** — full curl suite against a live server: all 32 checks passed, covering generated/custom codes, 409 duplicates, eleven 422 cases (malformed JSON, missing/invalid url, bad codes), 302 + exact `Location`, exact-once click counting, ascending listing, and 404s. I also killed and restarted the server: data and click counts survived (2 → 2 → 3), migrations re-applied idempotently, and start.sh correctly rebuilt the binary when missing. Server stopped; no stray processes."
  }
